00:26:08,460 --> 00:26:10,620
Burn him to ash, Misery!

266
00:26:13,760 --> 00:26:15,240
Eustass, do it already!

267
00:26:17,600 --> 00:26:18,430
What's that?

268
00:26:18,940 --> 00:26:21,240
Telling me what to do again, Trafalgar!

269
00:26:21,540 --> 00:26:23,893
Just sit there and keep your mouth shut!

270
00:26:42,400 --> 00:26:49,100
I'm not scared of you, you nasty boy, give
me your worst, you can't beat Big Mom!

271
00:26:50,360 --> 00:26:52,340
Keep telling yourself that!

272
00:26:53,680 --> 00:26:55,160
Now jump!

273
00:26:55,800 --> 00:26:56,630
Mom!

274
00:26:57,860 --> 00:26:59,540
You don't rule in our era.

275
00:27:22,140 --> 00:27:28,300
You pulled out all the stops this
time, honestly, I'm impressed.

276
00:27:34,740 --> 00:27:37,120
You boys must really like me.

277
00:27:38,740 --> 00:27:41,480
You don't want our time together to end,

278
00:27:41,680 --> 00:27:44,197
even though you can
barely stand on your feet.

279
00:27:44,280 --> 00:27:45,920
You're young, of course.

280
00:27:46,120 --> 00:27:47,920
You've got lots of energy.

281
00:27:48,460 --> 00:27:52,560
But I'm made of much
sterner stuff than you.

282
00:27:53,120 --> 00:27:56,317
You plants probably thought
you'd driven me to the brink.

283
00:27:56,400 --> 00:27:59,340
But try as you might, you can't defeat me.

284
00:28:02,660 --> 00:28:03,820
She's not dead?

285
00:28:04,020 --> 00:28:06,020
What the hell is it going to take?

286
00:28:06,120 --> 00:28:09,649
They've been kicking her ass,
but now she's laughing it all?

287
00:28:09,740 --> 00:28:10,840
Come on, boss!

288
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:13,200
This is insane!

289
00:28:14,360 --> 00:28:16,419
Kid and the captain are both spent.

290
00:28:16,560 --> 00:28:17,390
We're screwed!

291
00:28:18,120 --> 00:28:23,700
And when I do, your miserable little
lives will be putty in my hands!

292
00:28:24,020 --> 00:28:26,020
I'll grant you what mercy.

293
00:28:26,380 --> 00:28:28,620
You may choose your punishment.

294
00:28:29,540 --> 00:28:33,120
Would you like to hand over
50 years of your lifespan?

295
00:28:33,660 --> 00:28:37,400
Or would you rather stay
as you are and be my slave?

296
00:28:41,240 --> 00:28:44,960
Will it be life or slave?

297
00:28:49,380 --> 00:28:51,060
It's your son of a gun!

298
00:28:51,620 --> 00:28:53,040
That's enough, boss!

299
00:28:53,300 --> 00:28:54,420
We gotta book it!

300
00:28:57,120 --> 00:28:58,280
It's not fair!

301
00:28:58,500 --> 00:29:00,197
She's taking her life back to you!

302
00:29:00,280 --> 00:29:02,400
Stop it! My life! My life!

303
00:29:15,570 --> 00:29:16,400
Don't say anything but this!

304
00:29:16,483 --> 00:29:17,313
I thought she was gonna die!

305
00:29:17,396 --> 00:29:18,718
Then she turns around and does this!

306
00:29:18,820 --> 00:29:20,040
She's a monster!

307
00:29:21,260 --> 00:29:22,420
You've got to run!

308
00:29:22,720 --> 00:29:24,420
Get away from here, Captain!

309
00:29:32,540 --> 00:29:34,000
You guys should run.

310
00:29:35,540 --> 00:29:36,820
What a joke!

311
00:29:37,080 --> 00:29:38,374
She thinks I'm scared!

312
00:29:40,140 --> 00:29:42,300
I'm not giving you a damn thing.

313
00:29:42,720 --> 00:29:44,820
And I'll never be your slave.

314
00:29:45,140 --> 00:29:46,860
This is just a bluff.

315
00:29:47,660 --> 00:29:50,366
You've got one foot in
the grave, you old hag,

316
00:29:50,520 --> 00:29:53,344
and your half-assed threats
don't intimidate me!

317
00:29:55,760 --> 00:29:57,260
I can't believe it!

318
00:29:57,460 --> 00:30:00,677
Not even a second of their
lifespan has been taken away!

319
00:30:00,760 --> 00:30:02,437
He's in everywhere on the sea!

320
00:30:02,520 --> 00:30:05,108
You're telling me they're
not scared at all?

321
00:30:09,000 --> 00:30:09,830
Roronoa.

322
00:30:11,780 --> 00:30:16,604
As much as I'd like to relish my victory,
the dying screams will probably ruin it.

323
00:30:16,860 --> 00:30:21,300
Unless I do this, a gift
from the man who saved me.

324
00:30:25,580 --> 00:30:29,140
Stop being such a sore loser
and take a hit, damn it!

325
00:30:29,360 --> 00:30:31,160
The underworld is waiting!

326
00:30:31,580 --> 00:30:34,180
Let me help you on your way! It's silence!

327
00:30:37,860 --> 00:30:38,690
Huh?

328
00:30:38,800 --> 00:30:40,682
Is something wrong with my ears?

329
00:30:47,360 --> 00:30:48,920
Scream into the void.

330
00:30:49,200 --> 00:30:50,318
We've heard enough.

331
00:30:50,880 --> 00:30:53,380
This technique cancels out all sound.

332
00:30:57,720 --> 00:30:59,680
Sorry, didn't catch that.

333
00:31:00,220 --> 00:31:01,220
What's happening?

334
00:31:01,520 --> 00:31:02,740
My voice is gone!

335
00:31:04,460 --> 00:31:06,740
Captain, look behind you!

336
00:31:09,600 --> 00:31:11,897
And one more for the road!

337
00:31:11,980 --> 00:31:14,240
Jump off!

338
00:31:48,340 --> 00:31:52,257
Prometheus, Hera, what are you doing,

339
00:31:52,340 --> 00:31:56,037
why aren't you helping me,

340
00:31:56,120 --> 00:32:00,480
what,

341
00:32:00,920 --> 00:32:07,620
that big mom, what happened,
everything's silent,

342
00:32:09,840 --> 00:32:12,640
Nothing I touch makes a sound!

343
00:32:13,160 --> 00:32:16,580
What the hell have you
done to me, Trafalder?

344
00:32:17,200 --> 00:32:18,680
Let it go!

345
00:32:28,620 --> 00:32:30,100
He's gonna blow!

346
00:32:49,320 --> 00:32:50,257
What?

347
00:32:50,340 --> 00:32:52,040
Is that smoke?

348
00:32:52,440 --> 00:32:53,880
What's going on?

349
00:32:55,740 --> 00:32:58,400
Curse those stupid brats.

350
00:32:58,980 --> 00:33:01,620
And curse you too, Roger.

351
00:33:05,780 --> 00:33:10,117
you just couldn't keep
your mouth shut why the

352
00:33:10,200 --> 00:33:13,660
hell did you have to go and
say that before you died

353
00:33:18,640 --> 00:33:25,180
so you all want my treasure well you
can go ahead and have it it's out there

354
00:33:26,460 --> 00:33:30,220
i left it in one place now
you just have to find it

355
00:33:35,640 --> 00:33:37,440
People ain't bad up.

356
00:33:37,700 --> 00:33:39,660
The whole world bought into it.

357
00:33:44,160 --> 00:33:48,040
You've started the
so-called great pirate era.

358
00:33:48,360 --> 00:33:49,595
But what do you care?

359
00:33:49,700 --> 00:33:50,540
You're dead.

360
00:33:50,840 --> 00:33:52,546
It's not your problem, is it?

361
00:33:59,860 --> 00:34:04,560
All these brats got fired up thanks
to your little speech, Roger.

362
00:34:09,040 --> 00:34:12,860
And the pirates you left
behind from your generation,

363
00:34:13,140 --> 00:34:15,611
we're the ones who have to deal with them.

364
00:34:36,300 --> 00:34:38,380
That doesn't sound good!

365
00:34:38,800 --> 00:34:40,460
We need to leave now!

366
00:34:41,160 --> 00:34:42,620
Is there anyone there?

367
00:34:43,500 --> 00:34:45,360
What was that noise?

368
00:34:45,880 --> 00:34:47,440
Someone answer me!

369
00:34:52,520 --> 00:34:53,350
Oh, my

370
00:34:53,433 --> 00:34:59,900
God.

371
00:35:04,760 --> 00:35:05,590
Oh, my God.

372
00:35:05,673 --> 00:35:06,503
Ah!

373
00:35:12,460 --> 00:35:13,860
Water!

374
00:35:15,220 --> 00:35:16,620
Water!

375
00:35:23,620 --> 00:35:27,417
it's not fair otter you should have told

376
00:35:27,500 --> 00:35:31,180
us before you left this
world the one piece

377
00:35:32,240 --> 00:35:39,040
is the treasure even real
what is it where is it

378
00:35:40,060 --> 00:35:44,240
it could be right beneath my
nose and i wouldn't have a clue

379
00:35:45,700 --> 00:35:47,760
It's so frustrating

380
00:35:59,920 --> 00:36:00,960
Kid

381
00:36:03,160 --> 00:36:07,317
You won't get away with this My story

382
00:36:07,400 --> 00:36:11,297
isn't over It can't be Not like this,

383
00:36:11,380 --> 00:36:15,800
dammit I won't die Not from this!

384
00:36:16,080 --> 00:36:20,620
Mark my words, I will be back!

385
00:36:33,060 --> 00:36:37,707
The battle between Emperor of the Sea
Big Mom and the New Generation has ended.

386
00:36:40,300 --> 00:36:43,457
On the performance floor Inside the Skull

387
00:36:43,540 --> 00:36:47,100
Dome A cheer rings out
The winners are clear

388
00:36:53,380 --> 00:36:58,300
After a desperate struggle
Eustass Captain Kidd

389
00:36:59,940 --> 00:37:03,337
And his ally The Surgeon of Death

390
00:37:03,420 --> 00:37:08,400
Trafalgar Law are victorious at last.

391
00:37:09,280 --> 00:37:11,040
You did it, boss!

392
00:37:13,420 --> 00:37:14,340
Captain!

393
00:37:15,700 --> 00:37:17,360
You beat a new prophecy!

394
00:37:18,300 --> 00:37:19,560
This is a big deal!

395
00:37:19,720 --> 00:37:21,480
A really big deal!

396
00:37:38,560 --> 00:37:39,390
I see.

397
00:37:39,473 --> 00:37:40,417
So it's you.

398
00:37:40,500 --> 00:37:42,040
But why have you come?

399
00:37:48,920 --> 00:37:49,837
All right.

400
00:37:49,920 --> 00:37:51,744
This will do for now, at least.

401
00:37:53,160 --> 00:37:53,990
Wow!

402
00:37:54,073 --> 00:37:56,780
I knew you could do it,
Momonosuke! Keep it up!

403
00:37:58,300 --> 00:37:59,397
Yamato, it's you!

404
00:37:59,480 --> 00:38:02,020
Is that the basement? Oh no!

405
00:38:02,360 --> 00:38:03,380
It's exposed!

406
00:38:04,200 --> 00:38:05,700
It's been a real mess.

407
00:38:05,920 --> 00:38:07,567
Big Mom just set off a bomb.

408
00:38:07,780 --> 00:38:09,309
It blew out half the wall.

409
00:38:10,220 --> 00:38:11,797
I saw the explosion earlier.

410
00:38:11,880 --> 00:38:13,645
So that was her doing, was it?

411
00:38:14,280 --> 00:38:15,110
Uh-huh.

412
00:38:15,193 --> 00:38:17,297
I'm lucky the whole armory didn't explode.

413
00:38:17,380 --> 00:38:21,027
I was able to freeze everything,
so we should be safe for now.

414
00:38:22,160 --> 00:38:22,990
That's good news.

415
00:38:23,073 --> 00:38:25,215
I'm glad to see that you are unharmed.

416
00:38:26,600 --> 00:38:30,541
I'm still fighting to do my part,
but I need to tell you something.

417
00:38:31,680 --> 00:38:34,160
We have a very large visitor coming

418
00:38:35,180 --> 00:38:37,360
Are you familiar with Zunesha?

419
00:38:37,660 --> 00:38:38,960
The giant elephant?

420
00:38:39,340 --> 00:38:41,987
The same one Odin wrote
about in his journal?

421
00:38:42,280 --> 00:38:43,110
Impossible

422
00:38:58,560 --> 00:39:03,020
Zunesha was a companion of Joy Boy
who committed a crime 800 years ago.

423
00:39:03,580 --> 00:39:05,020
What could it all mean?
